<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended October 23, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Oct 23  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.11   -0.308    +0.657</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     2.32   -4.992    -7.208</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	462.37   -1.577    +5.982</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 149.10   -1.500   -17.500</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  29.75   -0.076    +0.713</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Chartered bank assets			   Sept	   Aug</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-12.32	-11.24</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     653.15	640.42</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    102.95	102.78</p>
<p>					  Sept 96     Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p>M1					 63.97	63.50	58.36</p>
<p>M2					390.60     389.11     382.89</p>
<p>M3					484.49     482.42     466.11</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
